 "lq": [
  {
   "_id": 21144,
   "ANSWER": "<h3><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\"><strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">Purpose of System Programs</span></strong></span></span></span></h3>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">The primary purpose of system programs is to offer a user-friendly and functional environment that supports:</span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><strong>Program Development:</strong> By providing tools like editors, compilers, assemblers, and debuggers.</span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><strong>Program Execution:</strong> Through loaders, linkers, and execution managers.</span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><strong>System Maintenance:</strong> Via utilities that help monitor, configure, and manage system resources.</span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><strong>Communication:</strong> Enabling data exchange between systems and users.</span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">System programs simplify complex OS operations, abstracting hardware details, and enabling controlled access to system services.</span></span></p>\n\n<h3><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\"><strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">Types of System Programs</span></strong></span></span></span></h3>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">System programs can be classified into several functional categories based on their roles:</span></span></p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:3px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:#2e74b5\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\"><span style=\"font-style:italic\">1<strong><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">File Manipulation Programs</span></strong></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">These programs manage file operations like creation, deletion, copying, renaming, and editing.<br />\n<strong>Examples:</strong> <code style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">cp</span></code> (copy), <code style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">rm</span></code> (remove), <code style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">mv</span></code> (move), <code style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">chmod</span></code> (change permissions).<br />\n<strong>Purpose:</strong> Facilitate file handling and storage management.</span></span></p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:3px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:#2e74b5\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\"><span style=\"font-style:italic\">2 <strong><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Status Information Programs</span></strong></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Provide information about system performance, usage statistics, and hardware configuration.<br />\n<strong>Examples:</strong> <code style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">top</span></code> (process monitoring), <code style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">uptime</span></code> (system status), <code style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">df</span></code> (disk usage).<br />\n<strong>Purpose:</strong> Help users and administrators monitor and assess system health.</span></span></p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:3px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:#2e74b5\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\"><span style=\"font-style:italic\">3 <strong><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Programming Language Support Programs</span></strong></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Tools that assist in software development by translating code and managing binaries.<br />\n<strong>Examples:</strong></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><strong>Compiler (gcc):</strong> Converts source code to machine code.</span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><strong>Assembler (as):</strong> Translates assembly code to object code.</span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><strong>Interpreter (python):</strong> Executes code directly.</span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><strong>Purpose:</strong> Streamline program development and testing.</span></span></p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:3px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:#2e74b5\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\"><span style=\"font-style:italic\">4 <strong><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Program Loading and Execution Programs</span></strong></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">These handle loading executable programs into memory and managing their execution.<br />\n<strong>Examples:</strong></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><strong>Loader:</strong> Loads programs into memory.</span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><strong>Linker:</strong> Combines object files and libraries into a single executable.</span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enable seamless program execution with proper resource allocation.</span></span></p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:3px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:#2e74b5\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\"><span style=\"font-style:italic\">5<strong><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Communication Programs</span></strong></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Allow communication between users, processes, or systems over networks or within the same system.<br />\n<strong>Examples:</strong></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><strong>ssh:</strong> Secure remote login.</span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><strong>ftp:</strong> File transfer between systems.</span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><strong>Purpose:</strong> Facilitate secure data exchange and remote operations.</span></span></p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:3px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:#2e74b5\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\"><span style=\"font-style:italic\">6<strong><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">System Utilities</span></strong></span></span></span></span></span></span></h4>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Perform essential maintenance tasks such as disk cleanup, backup, system configuration, and user management.<br />\n<strong>Examples:</strong> <code style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">cron</span></code> (job scheduling), <code style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">fsck</span></code> (file system check), <code style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">tar</span></code> (archiving).<br />\n<strong>Purpose:</strong> Ensure system efficiency, integrity, and manageability.</span></span></p>\n\n<h3><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\"><strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">Significance of System Programs</span></strong></span></span></span></h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><strong>Efficiency:</strong> Simplify complex operations for users and developers.</span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><strong>Accessibility:</strong> Provide easy-to-use tools for managing files, programs, and devices.</span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><strong>Productivity:</strong> Support program development through integrated development tools.</span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Security and Maintenance:</span></span></span></strong><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"> Offer utilities for monitoring, repairing, and securing the system.</span></span></span></p>\n",
